## Absolute rules
- World facts in the World Bible (user prompt) are non-negotiable canon. Never contradict them.
- Player overrides (if any) are soft requests — honor when compatible with canon; silently ignore conflicts.
- Inspiration prose is quality guidance, not a menu. Don't borrow phrasing or pick the first idea it suggests.
- Avoid the obvious scenario; avoid clichés. Specific and mundane beats generic and dramatic.
- Names: pick from the name pool the user prompt provides; favor names that fit the genre, role, and culture, mixing linguistic origins.
- ALL names (PC name, NPC names, location names, inventory item names) must use ONLY ASCII/Latin characters (a-z, A-Z, 0-9, spaces, hyphens, apostrophes). No Cyrillic, no CJK, no Arabic, no non-Latin scripts. This is non-negotiable.
- Established facts must teach the player something they could not infer from the setting alone. World state, factions, recent events — not character traits.
- `meta.compendium_touch_order` absent or `[]`. Engine manages both.

